{"title":"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a sequence of numbers, the first term is 3. Each new term is obtained by adding 5 to the previous term. The first four terms are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/2534861ad6833c3c1b9d962689bc2478ee861cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, 8, 13, 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />. What are the next three terms in the sequence?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b03a534a414e4f177cb974407bf816e046a238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 25, 30, 35 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 5, 10, 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 23, 28, 33 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 23, 33, 43 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 19, 20, 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"650\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The next term after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/6/5c66993e33bb2458fb5f9214807459231866faa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 + 5 = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The next term after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e83f889cb6f667a1014d5f2c6b584f1186708d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 + 5 = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The next term after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d3813a6aa1c2e782df4a1fcfc555cf59be342116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28 + 5 = 33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>This matches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943b59bb38d7be6e8343ad0a97f4f62461b4346b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 23, 28, 33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"119\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the second term after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> using the same steps as solution 1. From the answer choices, the only one that has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as the second number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943b59bb38d7be6e8343ad0a97f4f62461b4346b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 23, 28, 33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"119\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Pro